        <p>Clerk to the Guardians, Bewsey Chambers, August, 1808.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON UNION.-TENDH.- PERSONS WILLING to Contract for the aupply of any of the undermentioned articles from Michaelmas to Lady Day next, to be delivered free of expense at the Workhouse, or Cottage Homes situated at Padget° at such times and in such quantities as the Guardians or their officers may require, are requested to send in tenders to me on or before luesday September 4th, 1906. Tenders are required for : Milk for Workhouse</p>
        <p>Milk for Schools For 12 months. Coal and Slack Fish and ice Clogs Groceries and Necessaries Shoes and Slippers B nchers' Meat Coffins Officers Joints Looms and !truth, Flour and patinas! Leather and Shoemakers' Bread for Cottage Homes Necessaries Drapery Tailors Goods Wines and Spirits</p>
        <p>For 6 months. Feparate Tenders must be sent for the Workhouse and Cottage Homes, and samples of the articles required can be seen at either ,nstitution. The fuel to be supplied murt be anording to the specifica- tion as set forth on the tender form anti quotations must be made for delivery either to the new siding adjoining the, Workhouse or by cart.</p>
        <p>Forms of tender, and instructions to perzOns tendering, which must be strictly complied with, or any other informa- tion, may be obtained from the Maiter of the Workhouse,and the Superintendent of the Cottage Homes respectively, between the hours of 13 cm. and 4 p.m. The Guardians do hot necessarily bind themselves to accept the lowest or any tender. By order, JAMES C. SIIITOE.</p>
