      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-08-25_WidnesExaminer_art0025" n="art0025">
        <head>AXOTHER MUSICAL PRODIGY.</head>
        <p>AXOTHER MUSICAL PRODIGY.</p>
        <p>Yet another musical prodigy This-- time she hails from Melbourne. Her name is Leila Doubleday; she is only thirteen; and she is credited with wondrous Skill alike at the piano and with the violin. Her iends have organtsed' concerts in the chief Australian, cities. and £l.ood has already been secured. Fifty admirers have promised to subscribe each a guinea a year for five years to aid in her -musical education in Loudon.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-08-25_WidnesExaminer_art0026" n="art0026">
        <head>WHAT IS WORN.</head>
        <p>WHAT IS WORN.</p>
        <p>Yachting, boating, and travelling costumes now occupy the attention of our dressmakers when they are not busy with toilets, for couutry wear, which, the Laely says. are very similar in style. A zdft lettuce-green is now mixed ,with dark blue, instead of the brighter green forrheriy used, hut chalk and oyster-white in cloth, moire, and silk are much in favour for vests, collars; and faciags, and these are braided or em- broidered. Very narrow braids in different colours arc used closely grouped and Well ar- ranged, these forming charming trimmings.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-08-25_WidnesExaminer_art0027" n="art0027">
        <head>JAPANESE SILK BLOUSE.</head>
        <p>A JAPANESE SILK BLOUSE.</p>
        <p>The sketch shows our old friend the Japanese silk blouse in yet another style. This blouse can be made with or without a foundation, but in any case the puff sleeves should:have a lining to hold them in place. The blouse consists of a tucked- back, and a front tucked yoke depth, opening over a vest of the same silk tucked hori- zontally. The fastenings can be effeeted on the</p>
        <p>left aide of this front, which is bordered with bands of hand ewbroidery in delicate shades of mauve and • grelen and tiny pleated silk frills, while a bunch of mauve betse ribbon finishes oti the collar on 'either tide. The puffs of the sleeves are somewhat shorter than we have been wearing in blouse slips, and they are finished with tight cuffs, decorated to correspond with the front.</p>
