      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-08-25_WidnesExaminer_art0096" n="art0096">
        <head>Good Example.</head>
        <p>A Good Example.</p>
        <p>It is to be hoped that the example of the Chief Constable of Lan:irks-hire, who has lately•issued the following notice, ,will be larOly followed by police officers in other,distriets. • The notice runs " In every part of the county the Chief constable has noticed that the rule that vehicles should, keep to the left side of, the road is seldom complied with by any class of vehicle, whether heavy farm cart or private carriage. Now that motor cal* are becoming so common, the neglect of this fule is exceedingly dangerous, and the cause of many accidents Constables are to take every oppor- tunity of checking drivers who do ,not keep to the left side of, the road,"</p>
        <p>3 28, 7 20, 8 45, 98, 10 23 p.m. Sundays 843 a.m. 65,6 0, 9 54p.m . Widnes (C.L.C.)-7 5, 95, 10 0, 11 5 a.m. 12 0, al 0, bl 8, 2 5, 3 23, 4 10, 5 28, 6 28, 7 5, 80, 9 0, nlO 0, blO 37 p.m. a Saturdays only, b baturdp ys excepted.</p>
