        <p>DISTINCTIONS. The following, arranged in order of merit, obtained distinction :</p>
        <p>Botany (1 candidate.) C. Costello, Widnes. PASS LIST.</p>
        <p>First Division, framed on the aggregate work of the candidates, ond containing the names of those born on or after July 1, 1892, who satisfied the examiners ; arranged in numerical order under the several centres (1,271 candidates) : Widnes.—E. E. Clarke and H. C. Tracy,High School, Hough Green; C. Costello, St. Edward's Roman Catholic School, Runcorn; I. Riley, Union Buildings, High-street, Runcorn. Warrington.—E. Armstrong Carter, E. J. Dennett,and D. Williams, Prior School ; K. Grocott, R. Kilshaw, and G. Whitlow, High School, Stockton Heath ; A. M. Mouncey and I. M. Tunstall, Kirkfield School, Newton- le-Willows.</p>
        <p>Second Division, containing the names of the candi- dates who, having exceeded the age of fourteen years and not having exceeded the age of fifteen years on July 1, 1906, satisfied the examiners (1,145 candidates) : Widnes. —A. L. Kidd, Secondary School ; L. Boydell, High School, Hough Green. Warrington.—C. McG. Deas and M. G. Horton, High School, Stockton Heath; N. Nixon, Priory School, Warrington.</p>
        <p>DISTINCTIONS, Botany (1 candidate).—C. Costello, Widnes.</p>
