n of 0,716 for I grants and receipts the call would be only a:11,711 This would necessitate a rate of Gil. in the •.—A. , letter was read from Mr. F. H. Aukland asking for a I revision of his salary as relieving officer of No. 3 , district. The matter was referred to the next special; meeting of the Board. Mr. Mather stated that inl accordance with the Board's instructions, Mrs. Clay i and he had visited two Roman Catholic institutions with a view to ascertaining on what terms children could be sent there from the Padgate Homes, if it was considered necessary. At present the matter was not urgent so he would defer his report until the next meeting.—The master said Mr. Jenner Fast had told him that at Culcheth there were two homes empty— Mr. Mather: The birth rate must be low there (laughter).—lt was decided that a report should be presented to the Schools Committee before any other institutions were visited.— On the recommendation of i the House Committee it was resolved to enforce the : 'full detention of all vagrants and the completion of allotted tasks, and to utilize an adjoining room for ' sleeping accommodation, should necessity arise.</p>
